# Copy to tests/servicenow/.env (gitignored) and chmod 600 it, to run
# cmd/pleiades's ServiceNow release gate (TestServiceNowRunbookReleaseGate)
# against a real ServiceNow instance instead of ServiceNo!, the local mock
# of the Table API (tests/serviceno) it uses when these are unset. It holds
# a password, so keep it readable by you alone.
#
# A personal developer instance (PDI) is free: sign in at
# developer.servicenow.com and request one. It sleeps when it has not been
# used for a while and is reclaimed after a longer stretch of no use; wake it
# from the developer portal before a run, or the gate's first call fails.
#
# The gate makes ordinary Table API calls with basic authentication. It
# creates two configuration items (cmdb_ci) and three incidents whose names
# carry a random suffix, reads them, lets the runbook write work notes, reads
# those back from sys_journal_field, and deletes every record it created
# when it ends. The account must be able to create, read, update and delete
# incident and cmdb_ci records and read sys_journal_field; a PDI's own admin
# account can. On a shared instance, use a dedicated account limited to
# that. The devices the runbook collects from are still local sshd
# containers, so Docker must be running too.
#
# Run it with the variables exported, from the module root:
#
#   set -a; . tests/servicenow/.env; set +a
#   go test ./cmd/pleiades -run TestServiceNowRunbookReleaseGate -count=1 -v
#
# The instance's own URL: https and the host, no path.
PLEIADES_SNOW_INSTANCE=https://dev000000.service-now.com
# The account the gate signs in as, and its password.
PLEIADES_SNOW_USER=admin
PLEIADES_SNOW_PASSWORD=
